  "step_3": "The decision reason requires calculating an aspiration level as the mean of all outcomes (ignoring probabilities) and then comparing the probabilities of exceeding this level. The individual did not reference any such calculation or reference point. Instead, the individual focused only on the certainty of winning in B versus the risk in A. While both the decision reason and the individual end up favoring Lottery B, the justification processes differ fundamentally. The individual did not consider differences from an aspiration level or evaluate outcomes relative to such a benchmark. Therefore, although the final preference aligns with the decision reason, the reasoning process described does not reflect the use of the aspiration-level mechanism. The information considered and the justification rule applied by the individual do not match those required by the decision reason.",
  "final_assessment_score": 20
