  "step_3": "The decision reason requires (1) computing an aspiration level as the mean of all outcomes ignoring probabilities (-2250), (2) identifying which outcomes exceed this level (only 0 does), and (3) preferring the lottery with the higher chance of such positive differences (Lottery B, with 99.9%). The individual does not mention or imply any calculation of an average outcome, nor do they reference a threshold or aspiration level against which outcomes are compared. They do not evaluate how often an outcome exceeds a reference point. Instead, their reasoning is based on a direct comparison of worst-case losses and their personal tolerance for them, favoring the smaller potential loss despite its slightly higher probability. This aligns more with a minimax or loss-aversion heuristic than with the aspiration-level rule described. There is no evidence that the individual considered the concept of positive deviations from a computed aspiration level. Therefore, the decision reason was not used.",
